<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.14.1: Evaluating Quadratic Functions in the Real World</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01989</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.14.1: Evaluating Quadratic Functions in the Real World</md:title>
    <md:uuid>55c1d375-5819-43ef-bbc9-5559f1d23eed</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <para id="para-00001">The height, in inches, of a frog's jump is modeled by the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>75</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>, where the time <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, after the frog jumps, is measured in seconds.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">
          <media alt="close-up of a frog on plant stem">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_16_02_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        
    </para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>For <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>60</m:mn><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>75</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math>:</item>
      </list>
      <section id="sect-00002">
        <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_67eec057-f46f-4f3c-887c-aad2d0a7c8a2" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00003">Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00005">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_09870dcf-34f0-4827-b8a6-03b437b7fe10" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00006">Find <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00008">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00009">What do these values of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>h</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0.8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> mean in terms of the frog's jump?</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00010">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00011">They mean that the frog is on the ground when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (before jumping) and when <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0.8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (when the frog lands on the ground).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section  id="sect-00003">
        <exercise id="_1fe24a64-efa0-46d4-9188-efa86198aa89" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00012">After it jumped, how much time passed, in seconds, before the frog reached its maximum height?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00013">Correct! 0.4 seconds</para>
            <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is 0.4 seconds.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00015">Explain how you know this is the time the frog reached the maximum height.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00017">The frog reached its maximum height at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0.4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, as that is the halfway point of the jump. If we graph the function, the vertex of the graph will have a horizontal coordinate (<m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>t</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate) of 0.4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content></document>
